Conclusion:
This implementation uses an FSM to manage input handling and ensure synchronized control of the output. The design ensures:
•	Inputs are processed on the rising edge of the clock.
•	The output z stays at 0 until the user requests it using the enter signal.
The implementation achieves its goals by handling inputs and outputs in an organized, clock-synchronized way.

